## Usage

::: tabs

== Web editor

1. Go to a openEO Web Editor page e.g. https://openeofed.dataspace.copernicus.eu
1. Click on Log in at the bottom of the page if required.
1. Click on the `</> Code` button
1. Replace the content with this code
1. Modify the workflow and run the job

```json
{
  "process_graph": {
    "{{ model }}_embeddings1": {
      "process_id": "{{ model }}_embeddings",
      "namespace": "{{ process_graph_url }}",
      "description": "Documentation: {{ docs_url }}",
      "arguments": {
{% for parameter in required_parameters %}        "{{ parameter.name }}": {{ parameter.example_json }}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
{% endfor %}      }
    },
    "save1": {
      "process_id": "save_result",
      "arguments": {
        "data": { "from_node": "{{ model }}_embeddings1" },
        "format": "NETCDF"
      },
      "result": true
    }
  }
}
```

== Python

```python
import openeo

connection = openeo.connect("https://openeo.dataspace.copernicus.eu")
connection.authenticate_oidc()

embeddings = connection.datacube_from_process(
    "{{ model }}_embeddings",
    namespace="{{ process_graph_url }}",
{% for parameter in required_parameters %}    {{ parameter.name }}={{ parameter.example_python }},
{% endfor %})

job = embeddings.create_job(out_format="NETCDF")
job.start_and_wait()
job.download_result("{{ model }}_embeddings.nc")
```

== R

```r
library(openeo)

connect(host = "https://openeo.dataspace.copernicus.eu")
login()

# The R client cannot attach a process namespace URL to a node yet
# (Open-EO/openeo-r-client#143), so fetch the definition and bind its
# parameters locally instead. Start from the defaults the process declares,
# then override the required parameters.
definition <- jsonlite::fromJSON(
  "{{ process_graph_url }}",
  simplifyVector = FALSE
)
parameters <- lapply(definition$parameters, `[[`, "default")
names(parameters) <- vapply(definition$parameters, `[[`, "", "name")
{% for parameter in required_parameters %}parameters${{ parameter.name }} <- {{ parameter.example_r }}
{% endfor %}definition$parameters <- NULL

graph <- parse_graph(definition, parameters = parameters)

compute_result(
  graph = graph,
  format = "NETCDF",
  output_file = "{{ model }}_embeddings.nc"
)
```

